{"study_accession":"PRJNA529907","secondary_study_accession":"SRP190176","title":"CD71+ erythroid cells exacerbate HIV-1 infection via ROS and trans-infect HIV to CD4+ T cells","description":"We show that CECs originated from either the cord blood/placenta, peripheral blood of anemic and HIV patients mediate the exacerbation of HIV-1 replication in CD4+ T cells. Our observations coupled with RNAseq data demonstrate how interactions of CECs with CD4+ T cells via ROS affect the cell cycle machinery to facilitate HIV-1 replication. In addition, we demonstrate that CECs compared to mature RBCs express significantly higher levels of both CD35 and DARC, and can trans-infect HIV-1 to uninfected CD4+ T cells in vitro. Finally, our study indicates that HIV-1 interacts with CD235a on CECs and trans-infect uninfected CD4+ T cells in the presence of anti-retroviral drug, Tenofovir.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":4,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN11289223","study_accession":"PRJNA529907","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"infected1","description":"infected1","sex":"not collected","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2019-06-05","attributes":[["isolate","not collected"],["age","not collected"],["biomaterial_provider","not collected"],["sex","not collected"],["tissue","blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR8837339","experiment_accession":"SRX5625356","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":21959276,"base_count":6457129354,"first_public":"2019-06-05","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: RNAseq library of CD4 cells infected with HIV, repeat1"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN11289224","study_accession":"PRJNA529907","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"cocultured1","description":"cocultured1","sex":"not collected","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2019-06-05","attributes":[["isolate",